From 47bf1e342afa45fce74af407e78684b466818e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:58:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] llama : integrate the managed lazy reader into qwen4exp
 PLE

When --lazy-buffer-size > 0, load_arch_tensors creates a llama_lazy_reader
over the per_layer_token_embd.weight file range and skips the tensor's data
(TENSOR_SKIP). build_inp_ple then feeds an F32 graph input instead of a
get_rows node, and llm_graph_input_ple::set_input dequantizes the hashed
rows straight into it via lazy_reader->gather(). Layout matches the get_rows
output, so build_ple is untouched.

The mmap path stays the default (buf_size == 0). Also guards the loader
user path (llama_model_init_from_user has no weights_map): require_weight
calls become no-ops there and the PLE row count is derived from the head
ranges, which lets test-llama-archs build PLE fixtures from KV only.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
---
 src/llama-lazy-reader.cpp  | 11 ++---
 src/llama-lazy-reader.h    |  6 +++
 src/llama-model-loader.cpp |  8 +++-
 src/models/models.h        |  5 +++
 src/models/qwen4exp.cpp    | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 5 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

